# What `railway up` must NOT upload.
#
# Two jobs. The first is size: the CLI uploads this directory, and node_modules alone is
# larger than everything the API image needs. The second is detection: Railway builds with
# a Dockerfile when it finds one and otherwise falls back to Railpack, which reads the
# repository to guess a build. With the pnpm workspace in the upload, that guess was
# "Node monorepo workspace" — the wrong build entirely, and the reason an earlier deploy
# never touched the API Dockerfile. The Dockerfile now sits at the repository root where
# Railway looks first; keeping the JavaScript workspace out of the upload removes the
# fallback's input as well.
#
# The API image needs exactly two directories from this repository: apps/api (the service)
# and data (seed, taxonomy, and the AI Gateway's deterministic fallback snapshots, which
# app.core.config uses to locate the repository root inside the container).

# --- The web app and its toolchain: nothing the API image builds from --------
node_modules
apps/web
packages
.next
.turbo
package.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
pnpm-workspace.yaml
.npmrc
vercel.json

# --- Python host artefacts ---------------------------------------------------
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# --- Secrets: never leave the machine ----------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Version control, CI, docs, local tooling --------------------------------
.git
.github
docs
evals
docker-compose.yml
Makefile
make.ps1

# Root prose only. NOT `*.md`: apps/api/pyproject.toml names apps/api/README.md as its
# readme, and dropping a file a manifest points at is a build failure waiting for a
# quiet afternoon.
/*.md

# --- Local object storage: demo document bytes, not application code ---------
storage/*
!storage/.gitkeep

